Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 21:54:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: fix fan threshold milli-Celsius handling
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="------------false"

This is a multi-part message in MIME format.
--------------false
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=fixed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit


The PS4 fan threshold is exposed through hwmon as milli-Celsius, but the
underlying ICC thermal configuration stores the threshold as a plain
integer Celsius byte. The driver converted milli-Celsius to Celsius with
integer division, so a write such as 45500 was programmed as 45C while
the cached hwmon value remained 45500.

Reject non-integer Celsius milli-Celsius writes so the cached hwmon value
always matches what the hardware can represent. Keep the existing
read-modify-write protocol that preserves the full thermal configuration
and only changes the threshold byte.

This makes temp1_crit readback and duplicate-write handling consistent
with the PS4 fan controller's actual precision.

Signed-off-by: rmuxnet <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
---
 drivers/ps4/ps4-fan.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)


--------------false
Content-Type: text/x-patch; name="0083-ps4-fix-fan-threshold-milli-Celsius-handling.patch"
